From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Dichev <stefanbdichev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:32:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] core: reconnect the access point without invalidating the
 session

The server closes the access-point connection often, typically right
after a keep-alive Pong. The session was then invalidated, taking the
dealer and Spirc with it, so the device left Spotify Connect until the
application built a new session.

The session now runs its connection in one task. When the connection
closes, a write fails or the keep-alive times out, it logs in again on
the next access point with the reusable credentials and the session
stays valid. Packets sent meanwhile go out on the new connection,
pending audio-key requests are sent again, and mercury requests and
subscriptions and channels of the closed connection end. A failed
reconnect, or a connection that closes within 30 s of connecting,
still invalidates the session.

A timed-out audio-key request now leaves the pending map, so it is not
sent again after a reconnect.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013zyp13aMbmU4XmKnuCPVRb
